# CODEOWNERS example. Uncomment and replace the placeholders.
# GitHub requests review from the owners of every path a PR touches.
# The last matching pattern wins, so put broad rules first.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Keep owners as teams, not individuals, so reviews do not stall on one
# person's holiday. Pair this file with a branch rule that requires
# code-owner review only on the paths listed below the default.

# Default: the owning team reviews everything.
# *                       @your-org/service-team

# CI and quality gates: changes here affect every repo that calls them.
# /.github/workflows/      @your-org/platform-team

# Infrastructure and secrets handling.
# /infra/                  @your-org/platform-team
# /deploy/                 @your-org/platform-team

# Database migrations need a second pair of eyes for locking and rollback.
# /migrations/             @your-org/service-team @your-org/data-reviewers

# Standards and runbooks.
# /docs/                   @your-org/engineering-leads
